From d6b983aa16b83a533c3aae336b79d22b45c0be3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:56:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] glTF: Parse meshes in parallel

Distribute mesh parsing over the WorkerThreadPool in
GLTFDocument::_parse_meshes(). Each mesh is parsed independently into
a pre-allocated slot:

- Unique mesh names are pre-generated up front, since _gen_unique_name()
  mutates shared state.
- Per-mesh parse errors are collected and the first failure is
  propagated, preserving the original error behavior.
- Material mutation (vertex color flag) is serialized, as materials
  can be shared between meshes.
- When already running on a worker thread (e.g. a threaded scene
  import), meshes are parsed inline instead, avoiding nested group
  waits that can starve the pool.

Also make the extracted-image path import-thread aware: the file
system tree update is deferred to the main thread, and the decoded
source image is kept instead of reading the texture back from the
rendering server, which is only safe on the main thread.

Add a regression test that invalid mesh data fails parsing instead of
silently producing null meshes.
